{
  "_comment": [
    "The CIP catalog of go-ethernetip: object classes, services, status codes, data types and device types.",
    "It is the source of truth: `go generate ./...` (internal/cmd/gencatalog) writes cip/catalog_gen.go and CATALOG.md from it and from cip/vendors.json; CI fails when they drift.",
    "Numbers are strings in C notation (\"0x01\") so that the catalog reads like the tables of the specifications.",
    "ident is the Go identifier suffix: class Identity becomes cip.ClassIdentity, service Get_Attribute_Single cip.ServiceGetAttributeSingle, status 0x05 cip.StatusPathDestinationUnknown.",
    "source names where each entry is publicly documented; see CATALOG.md, Provenance. The ODVA specifications themselves are not redistributed."
  ],
